
Hyperledger Fabric + FabCar
===========================

1. Start the test network
-------------------------
cd ~/fabric-samples-old/test-network
./network.sh up

2. Create a channel
-------------------
./network.sh createChannel
# or for a specific name
./network.sh createChannel -c mychannel

3. Deploy FabCar chaincode
--------------------------
./network.sh deployCC -ccn fabcar -ccp ../fabcar/chaincode-go -ccl go
# or JavaScript version
./network.sh deployCC -ccn fabcar -ccp ../fabcar/chaincode-javascript -ccl javascript

4. Enroll Admin and Register User
---------------------------------
cd ~/fabric-samples-old/fabcar/javascript
node enrollAdmin.js
node registerUser.js

5. Start API Backend Server
---------------------------
cd ~/fabric-samples-old/fabcar/javascript/api
node server.js

# Expected:
# ✅ FabCar API is running at http://localhost:4000

6. REST API Commands (using curl or Postman)
--------------------------------------------

Register user:
--------------
curl -X POST http://localhost:4000/register \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"username":"gregoryUser"}'

Query all cars:
---------------
curl http://localhost:4000/cars

Create a car:
-------------
curl -X POST http://localhost:4000/createCar \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"carId":"CAR10","make":"Subaru","model":"Outback","colour":"silver","owner":"Gregory"}'

Change car owner:
-----------------
curl -X POST http://localhost:4000/changeOwner \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"carId":"CAR10","newOwner":"Alice"}'

7. Create Frontend (React + Vite)
---------------------------------
npm create vite@latest fabcar-frontend -- --template react
cd fabcar-frontend
npm install
npm run dev

# Vite homepage should show successfully.

Summary
-------
✅ Fabric network up
✅ FabCar chaincode deployed
✅ API backend built and running
✅ React frontend setup and working
✅ Commands for create, query, update (change ownership) tested successfully
